      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Figure 11: Closer look at comparison of algorithms in Safety MuJoCo Reacher and HalfCheetah Environments.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        392.6667785644531,
        504.00372314453125,
        400.6827392578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Note on HalfCheetah: The rewards for HalfCheetah are based on the absolute distance traveled in",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        415.7027893066406,
        503.99884033203125,
        424.7289123535156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "each step. Without the cost metric to constrain backward travel, it is easy to learn to run backward, as",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        426.7313537597656,
        504.00146484375,
        435.6379089355469
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "is the behavior learned in unconstrained PPO.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        437.6403503417969,
        290.146240234375,
        446.5469055175781
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "RESPO: Our approach achieves the highest reward performance among the safety baselines in",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        453.9097900390625,
        503.9967346191406,
        462.9359130859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "HalfCheetah and decent reward performance in Reacher. Interestingly, RESPO also has 0 constraint",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        464.7789611816406,
        503.9999084472656,
        473.84490966796875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "violations in HalfCheetah and the second lowest constraint violations in Reacher.",
      "bbox": [
        107.7509994506836,
        475.84735107421875,
        430.9775085449219,
        484.75390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "PPOLag: The performance in Reacher for PPOLag is similar as in most of the previous environments:",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        492.11578369140625,
        505.3836364746094,
        501.14190673828125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "decently high rewrad, cost near the threshold. However, for HalfCheetah, interesting PPOLag learns",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        503.0247802734375,
        503.9998779296875,
        512.0509033203125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "to maintain the violations well below the cost threshold.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        514.0533447265625,
        331.0725402832031,
        522.9598999023438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "RCRL: We see yet again RCRL has high reward follow by very high constraint violations.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        530.3228149414062,
        471.9232482910156,
        539.3489379882812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "FAC: This approach has decent reward performance in Reacher and low reward performance in",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        546.7108154296875,
        503.9959411621094,
        555.7369384765625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "HalfCheetah. However, interestingly, FAC has high cost violations though below the cost threshold.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        557.6207885742188,
        505.7383728027344,
        566.6469116210938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "CBF: In Reacher, the CBF approach has conservative behavior with both low reward and low cost",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        574.0087890625,
        503.995849609375,
        583.034912109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "violations. But in HalfCheetah, it has very low reward performance and very high cost violations (not",
      "bbox": [
        107.7509994506836,
        585.037353515625,
        503.99664306640625,
        593.9439086914062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "seen in the plot since its an order of magnitude larger than the visible range).",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        595.9463500976562,
        413.5628356933594,
        604.8529052734375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "CRPO, P3O, & PCPO: These CMDP-based primal approaches have decent reward performance in",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        612.2157592773438,
        503.9968566894531,
        621.2418823242188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Reacher while maintaining violations within cost threshold. In HalfCheetah, however, they achieve",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        623.244384765625,
        503.9970703125,
        632.1509399414062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "low performance and low cost violations.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        634.1533813476562,
        272.41278076171875,
        643.0599365234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Vanilla PPO: This unconstrained algorithm consistently has high rewards and high costs (sometimes",
      "bbox": [
        107.64099884033203,
        650.4227905273438,
        503.9969787597656,
        659.4489135742188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "out of the scope of the plots), so maximizing rewards does not improve costs in these environments.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        661.4513549804688,
        505.41802978515625,
        670.35791015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
